REGENT OF TOLITOLI,

Considering:
a. that violence against women and children is a crime against human rights so it becomes the obligation of the state to protect from all forms of violence and discrimination;
b. that to fulfill the rights of women and children as well as part of the regional government's efforts to protect women and children from exploitation, neglect and discrimination;
c. that to provide direction, foundation and legal certainty in the protection of women and children, regulation at the regional level is required;
d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b and letter c, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning the Protection of Women and Children Victims of Violence;

In View of:
1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;

2. Law Number 29 of 1959 concerning the Establishment of Level II Regions in Sulawesi (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1959 Number 74, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 1822);
3. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587) as amended several times most recently by Law Number 9 of 2015 concerning the Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2015 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5679);

With the Mutual Approval of THE REGIONAL HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES OF TOLITOLI REGENCY and

